 "title": "Group Anagrams",
 "slug": "group-anagrams",
 "category": "arrays-hashing",
 "difficulty": "Medium",
 "url": "https://leetcode.com/problems/group-anagrams/",
 "pattern": "Hash map keyed by a canonical form",
 "statement": "Given a list of strings, group the **anagrams** together (words made of exactly the same letters). The groups and the words inside them may be returned in any order.",
 "example": {
  "input": "strs = [\"eat\",\"tea\",\"tan\",\"ate\",\"nat\",\"bat\"]",
  "output": "[[\"eat\",\"tea\",\"ate\"],[\"tan\",\"nat\"],[\"bat\"]]",
  "why": "eat / tea / ate share the letters a, e, t; tan / nat share a, n, t; bat is alone."
 },
 "more": [
  {
   "input": "strs = [\"\"]",
   "output": "[[\"\"]]"
  },
  {
   "input": "strs = [\"a\"]",
   "output": "[[\"a\"]]"
  },
  {
   "input": "strs = [\"ab\",\"ba\",\"abc\"]",
   "output": "[[\"ab\",\"ba\"],[\"abc\"]]"
  }
 ],
 "idea": [
  "Anagrams contain exactly the same letters. We need a *label* that is identical for all anagrams and different for everything else.",
  "**Sort the letters** of a word: `eat`, `tea` and `ate` all become `aet`. That sorted string is the label.",
  "Use the label as a hash-map key and append each word to its key's list. Each list in the map is one group."
 ],
 "code": "class Solution:\n    def groupAnagrams(self, strs: List[str]) -> List[List[str]]:\n        anagrams_map = {}\n\n        for word in strs:\n            sorted_word = \"\".join(sorted(word))\n            if sorted_word in anagrams_map:\n                anagrams_map[sorted_word].append(word)\n            else:\n                anagrams_map[sorted_word] = [word]\n\n        return list(anagrams_map.values())",
 "complexity": {
  "time": "O(n · k log k)",
  "timeWhy": "n words, and sorting a word of length k costs k log k.",
  "space": "O(n · k)",
  "spaceWhy": "The map stores every word once."
 },
